# Agent Rules for EvidenceOS Web Frontend (TanStack Start + Meta StyleX + Vite+)

## 1. Zero Tailwind CSS Constraint
- STRICTLY FORBIDDEN: Do not use Tailwind CSS utility classes, `@tailwind` directives, `tailwind.config.js`, `postcss.config.js`, or `autoprefixer`.
- All styling MUST be implemented using Meta StyleX (`@stylexjs/stylex`).

## 2. Meta StyleX Conventions
- All component styles must be defined statically using `stylex.create({ ... })`.
- Apply styles to JSX elements using `{...stylex.props(styles.target)}`.
- Pass conditional styles as trailing arguments to `stylex.props()`:
  `stylex.props(styles.base, isActive && styles.active, isError && styles.error)`.
- Use design tokens from `src/styles/tokens.stylex.ts` whenever referencing theme colors, spacing, and border radii.
- Never use dynamic string concatenation or template literals for styles.
- Theme variable definitions must strictly reside in files ending in `*.stylex.ts`.
- Nest pseudo-classes and media queries inside property values (`color: { default: "...", ":hover": "..." }`) rather than top-level `":hover": { ... }`, and prefer longhand properties (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) over shorthands (`border`, `background`) per `@stylexjs/eslint-plugin`.

## 3. TanStack Start & Router Conventions
- Routes must use TanStack Router file-based conventions inside `src/routes/`.
- Use `createFileRoute('/path')` for route components.
- Use `Link` from `@tanstack/react-router` for internal navigation.
- Ensure all route loader outputs and search params maintain strict TypeScript typing.
- Never use Next.js conventions (`'use server'`, `app/api/route.ts`, `next/navigation`, `next/link`).

## 4. Agent Tooling & Verification Workflow
- Always verify code via `vp check` and `npm run build` in `apps/web`.
- Verify clean compilation with exit code 0 before concluding any changes.
